      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Coverage, thresholds and source",
      "description": "Original synthetic mask by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors (MIT). No external images. Pixel-cell area coverage is a software validity model, not physical camera calibration or proof of full cubic/Lanczos interpolation support. Carry first-stage fractional coverage to the next resize instead of thresholding it early. These aligned factor-two footprints make the fractional chain match the direct factor-four area calculation exactly. The thresholded-first branch loses valid area. General repeated fractional resizing of nonaligned grids is not equivalent to resampling the original; keep the original mask when accuracy across such chains matters.",
      "parameters": {},
